# .gitignore
# popo
#
# Copyright © 2026 Dagitali LLC. All rights reserved.
#
# Git ignore configuration for intentionally untracked repository files.
#
# Git is a distributed version control system that tracks changes in source
# code during software development. The `.gitignore` file allows you to
# define patterns for files and directories that should be ignored by Git.

# Responsibilities
# - Ignore build, cache, coverage, and virtual environment artifacts that
#   should not be committed.
# - Keep generated and local-only files out of source control by default.
# - Reduce accidental commits of transient development artifacts.
#
# Maintainer Notes
# - Keep ignore rules focused on this project's generated and local-only files.
# - Prefer narrow project-specific ignore rules when adding new local artifacts.
# - Do not ignore release artifacts that CI needs to build, audit, or publish
#   from tracked source files.
#
# References
# - Git ignore reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore

/.coverage
/.mypy_cache/
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.venv/
/build/
/dist/
/htmlcov/
/src/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
